WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.652
Immigration pathway comparison.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:05.056
Three roads to exploitation.

00:00:05.056 --> 00:00:10.784
Canada operates three major immigration pathways, each with a different exploitation mechanism.

00:00:10.784 --> 00:00:14.909
Express Entry selects for credentials it refuses to recognise.

00:00:14.909 --> 00:00:20.590
The Temporary Foreign Worker Program ties workers to employers who control their immigration status.

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:26.590
International student programs extract maximum tuition while providing uncertain pathways to permanence.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:37.068
All three pathways serve institutional interests: employers get cheaper labour, universities get tuition revenue, the housing market gets demand, and GDP headlines get population growth.

00:00:37.068 --> 00:00:44.909
The newcomers who travel these three roads share one destination: a system designed to extract maximum value while offering minimum protection.

00:00:44.909 --> 00:00:50.306
Comparison table: three immigration pathways and how each exploits newcomers differently.
